From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] texture cache: delete images whose memory went wholly to newer images (sbihaiko, Lichii #1314, EDEN_NX2_TC_SUPERSEDED), off by default

What: the game moves its render targets within a memory pool every frame while the camera moves
(sbihaiko counts about 45 images a frame in a later area). Each new one is a bad overlap of the
old ones, which stay registered until the age-based collector reaches them, far slower than they
arrive. EDEN_UP_STALE_TARGETS (0650) deletes drawn-over render targets the GPU wrote once unused
for 10 frames; this deletes, after 2 frames unused, any image that can be proven to hold nothing a
guest read or a join could still return.

With EDEN_NX2_TC_SUPERSEDED=1 (exact "1", read once, Switch 2 titles only): every frame within 3
frames of a new bad overlap (JoinImages) or a whole clear, TickFrame (after RetireStaleTargets,
before AreaEvict) walks the images unused for 2 frames that have bad overlaps and classifies each
(ClassifySuperseded, new header superseded_images.h, his, unchanged):
- Clean: it holds no GPU data (not IsSafeGpuCopy) and its whole range lies in newer images used
  after it: deleted.
- Rewritten: it holds GPU data and its whole range lies in newer GPU-written images that cleared
  their whole surface after its last write (full_write_tick, recorded by NoteWholeClears in
  UpdateRenderTargets for a clear): deleted without a download.
- Unproven (covered, but not by whole clears): kept, counted.
Excluded always: sparse, unbacked, unwritten-sparse, remapped, decoding, trimmed images, images with
aliases, CPU-modified covers. Ours: never an image something still needs, as 0650 keeps them
(CollectStaleReferences: a queued download, an asynchronous decode or unswizzle, a bound render
target, one of the last four presents; the present ring is now also recorded with this switch).
The deletion is the
collector's: untrack, unregister, DeleteImage (the memory waits for the GPU); not MarkStale (the
covering images hold the bytes). Line every 600 frames (HW_GPU): deleted, rewritten, unproven,
kept as still needed. Known limit (from Lichii): block-linear padding bytes that belong to no texel
count as covered.

ClearOverwritesWhole: his, with the clear-covers test of his parent core (surface clip, scissor,
lower-left flip) written into it, since our core has no ClearCovers member; our JoinImages'
overwritten_by_clear stays as it is.

Changed from his: exact "1" (his: anything but "0"); the switch helper sits before its first use
(his b93a1f9's fix); no PartialDownload exclusion (his 4386a82's: our core has no such flag); the
still-needed check (0650's); the 600-frame line is in DeleteSupersededImages; deletions are traced as
"superseded".

Off: two u64 image fields that stay 0 (16 bytes per image); one static bool test per PrepareImage,
per clear's UpdateRenderTargets, per JoinImages with bad overlaps, per present and per frame. Not in
the kept-store stamp.

Origin and credit: sbihaiko, EglantinePS5 branch b24-keeps, commits 91a301c (his 0917
EDEN_NX2_TC_SUPERSEDED), 4386a82 and b93a1f9; after zortos293/Lichii PR #1314.
